WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.270
I’ve been using Apple’s iPad Mini 5 for
the last 2 weeks, and I’ve realized that

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:09.330
it’s currently the best tablet for gaming,
topping every Android tablet and iPad for

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.980
a few different reasons, which I’ll get
into in a minute.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.610
It’s basically the same iPad as the new
iPad Air but in a smaller package.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.680
And the display is much improved from the
iPad Mini 4, with 500 nits of brightness,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.290
True Tone technology and p3 wide-color gamut
for incredible color accuracy for photo editing.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:32.470
And it now supports the Apple Pencil for taking
notes, drawing and more, adding tremendous

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.950
value compared to the old iPad Mini 4 which
was priced at the same $400.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.420
You really get so much more value with the
new iPad Mini 5, especially since you’re

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:47.370
going from the A8 processor in the Mini 4
to the A12 in the mini 5, which comes directly

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.679
from the iPhone XS and XS Max.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:54.660
So you’re getting iPhone XS performance
for only $400, and if you compare it to the

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.949
chips you get in the best android tablets
out there, it completely blows them out of

00:00:58.949 --> 00:00:59.949
the water.

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:04.720
In Geekbench 4’s single-core test, the iPad
Mini 5 basically triples the scores of the

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.040
Android tablets, and it’s the same story
for the multi-core test, tripling most of

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.580
the scores and almost doubling the score of
the Samsung Galaxy Tab S4, which retailed

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:22.800
at $780 but has quickly gone down to $530,
still more expensive than the iPad Mini 4.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.980
And finally, in Antutu’s graphics benchmark,
which is more accurate for gaming performance,

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.310
the iPad Mini 5 again easily outperforms the
Android tablets, almost doubling the score

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.330
of the Galaxy Tab S4.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.810
And that’s not the only difference.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:40.670
Many people know that iPads are more reliable,
perform better over time and hold their value

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.570
much better than Android tablets.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:49.410
Samsung’s $400 Galaxy Tab S5e is also coming
soon and it’s actually packing a similar

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:54.020
or slower chip than the Tab S4, so the iPad
Mini 5 is gonna be the clear winner in terms

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.950
of performance for 2019.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.350
Yes, the iPad Mini 5 is more expensive than
some of these Android tablets, but trust me,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.880
you won’t regret spending more.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.891
This iPad will give you years of reliable
performance.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.740
So the performance is definitely there, but
how is it better than the rest of Apple’s

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.110
current iPad lineup?

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:13.321
For starters, the iPad Mini’s size and weight
are perfect for comfortably holding it in

00:02:13.321 --> 00:02:19.500
your hand, for everything from browsing the
web, watching youtube videos, reading eBooks,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.150
taking notes, drawing, taking it on the go,
and especially for playing games.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:29.900
The rest of the iPads, even the 2018 budget
iPad, are heavier and much larger, making

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.560
them less comfortable to hold.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.499
For playing games, your hands will get tired
over time, and you don’t really get that

00:02:35.499 --> 00:02:36.959
with the iPad Mini 5.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.590
It basically packs all the iPad you’ll ever
need in a perfectly compact form factor.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.799
Now you might be asking, why don’t I just
get the cheaper 2018 iPad instead?

00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:50.120
Well, there are quite a few drawbacks with
that iPad, mainly with the display, and I

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.040
have a detailed video comparing them if you
want to learn more.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.580
But there’s also a significant difference
in gaming performance.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.279
Take Fortnite for example, the 2018 iPad can
only run the game at 30 frames per second

00:03:02.279 --> 00:03:03.650
on medium graphics.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.590
Not only that, but in game, the graphics are
noticeably worse, you’ll get dropped frames

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:13.359
so it won’t be perfectly smooth, and the
display is very reflective and not as bright,

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.879
which can get pretty annoying.

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:20.220
The iPad Mini 5 runs Fortnite at 60 frames
per second on high settings, and it’s incredibly

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:25.430
smooth, no noticeable dropped frames, no issues
with reflectivity, and you can play for hours

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.670
thanks to the small and light form factor,
which makes it a lot more portable as well.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:31.680
Now, what about the iPad Air and the 2018
iPad Pro?

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.489
Well, the iPad Air is basically a larger version
of the iPad Mini, there’s literally no difference

00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:38.620
in performance.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:43.099
The 2018 iPad Pro, is definitely a lot more
powerful than the iPad Mini 5, but it’s

00:03:43.099 --> 00:03:44.700
also twice as expensive.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.420
It’s fairly large so it’s not very comfortable
for long gaming sessions, and it’s overkill

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.650
for basically every game currently available
on the app store.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.650
How?

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:58.469
Well, in Fortnite, it’s limited to the exact
same graphics settings as the iPad Mini 5,

00:03:58.469 --> 00:04:04.579
and it runs it just as smooth, with no benefits
at all, even with all of that extra performance.

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:07.279
The story’s the same in other games like
Asphalt 9.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:12.439
You get 60 frames per second at maxed out
graphics and it runs perfectly smooth on both

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:15.249
the iPad Pro and iPad Mini 5.

00:04:15.249 --> 00:04:21.030
I also played some PUBG, and maxed out the
graphics on both iPads, and I mean max everything.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:27.030
HDR since Ultra HDR isn’t available yet,
ultra frame rate, anti-aliasing enabled and

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.199
auto-adjust graphics disabled.

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:34.420
The iPad Pro ran everything perfectly, except
it didn’t use up the whole display, just

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.840
like on Fortnite, there are black bars all
around that don’t get used.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:43.830
Either way, I managed to score an SSS on my
first match ever.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.330
On the iPad Mini 5, it also ran the game perfectly
with maxed out settings.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:52.460
Everything was super smooth, no issues at
all, but it was much more comfortable to hold

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.520
in the hand.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.530
This time, I scored an SS+, not bad for my
first two matches.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.550
So from those three graphically-demanding
games, we can see that the extra power of

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.030
the iPad Pro isn’t really being used compared
to the iPad Mini 5, and until we get some

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:12.190
new and very graphically-demanding games on
iOS, there won’t be any difference in gaming.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.900
Of course, you’ll see the difference in
tasks like video editing, but the average

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.099
user honestly won’t be able to tell the
difference in performance.

00:05:19.099 --> 00:05:24.032
And that’s why I’m calling the iPad Mini
5 the best gaming tablet in 2019, and for

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:27.250
only $400, it’s a really great deal for
what you get.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.319
And it’ll give you years of reliable performance
for all of your iPad needs.

00:05:31.319 --> 00:05:36.190
Now, if the display is too small for your
liking, you can pay $100 more for the new

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.190
iPad Air.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:42.280
It’s basically the same exact iPad, except
with a larger 10.5” display and a smart

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.020
connector for Apple’s smart keyboard.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.020
That’s it.

